This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - User started by asking to download superpowers skills by obra and reassess CloudDesk project
   - Project shifted from hackathon to personal project (study tool + agentic sandbox + portfolio piece)
   - **Agentic upgrade**: Make agents genuinely agentic — real tool use (Vercel AI SDK), multi-step reasoning (two-step debrief), all within free-tier Gemini (≤10 RPM)
   - **Multi-role feature**: Add Senior Developer and Team Lead roles alongside Solutions Architect; add 4 counterpart personas (client, non-tech, junior-dev, team-engineer); all roles get free counterpart picker
   - **Multi-cert feature (pending)**: Expand from AWS SAA-C03 to 5 Azure associate certifications (to be designed after multi-role implementation)

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Vercel AI SDK v6 (`ai@^6.0.205`, `@ai-sdk/google@^3.0.82`) — `generateText`, `tool()`, `stepCountIs`
   - **API breaking changes in ai v6**: `maxSteps` renamed to `stopWhen: stepCountIs(N)`; `parameters` renamed to `inputSchema` on `tool()`
   - Tool calling via closure factory: `buildScenarioTools(userModel)` captures userModel at call time
   - Two-step debrief pipeline: per-exchange scoring (temp 0.1) → synthesis (temp 0.2)
   - `sessionStorage` only (no DB), userModel snapshot sent in request body (server-side sessionStorage unavailable)
   - Adapter pattern: `lib/llm.ts` and `lib/speech.ts` are the ONLY provider-aware files — agents NEVER import provider SDKs directly
   - Markdown fence stripping (`stripFences()`) before `JSON.parse` on all LLM JSON responses
   - `counterpartRole` field in `ScenarioOutput` — set by scenario agent, read by meeting agent and brief card
   - Subagent-driven development with two-stage review (spec compliance + code quality)

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`lib/llm.ts`** — Fully rewritten to use Vercel AI SDK. Both `callLLM` and `callLLMWithTools` exported.
     ```typescript
     import { createGoogleGenerativeAI } from "@ai-sdk/google";
     import { generateText, stepCountIs } from "ai";
     import type { Message, LLMOpts, UserModel } from "./types";
     import { buildScenarioTools } from "./tools";
     const google = createGoogleGenerativeAI({ apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY! });
     const MODEL = google("gemini-2.5-flash");
     function toAIMessages(messages: Message[]) {
       const msgs = messages.length > 0 ? messages : [{ role: "user" as const, content: "Begin." }];
       return msgs.map((m) => ({ role: m.role as "user" | "assistant", content: m.content }));
     }
     // opts.json is intentional dead code — JSON output is enforced via prompt, not API flag
     export async function callLLM(systemPrompt: string, messages: Message[], opts: LLMOpts = {}): Promise<string> {
       const { text } = await generateText({ model: MODEL, system: systemPrompt, messages: toAIMessages(messages), temperature: opts.temperature ?? 0.8 });
       return text;
     }
     export async function callLLMWithTools(systemPrompt: string, messages: Message[], userModel: UserModel, opts: LLMOpts = {}): Promise<string> {
       const tools = buildScenarioTools(userModel);
       const { text } = await generateText({ model: MODEL, system: systemPrompt, messages: toAIMessages(messages), tools, stopWhen: stepCountIs(4), temperature: opts.temperature ?? 0.8 });
       return text;
     }
     ```

   - **`lib/tools.ts`** — Created. `buildScenarioTools(userModel)` factory with 3 tools using `inputSchema` (ai v6 API).
     ```typescript
     import { tool } from "ai";
     import { z } from "zod";
     import type { UserModel } from "./types";
     const AWS_SERVICE_PATTERN = /\b(EC2|S3|RDS|Lambda|DynamoDB|CloudFront|Route\s?53|VPC|IAM|KMS|ELB|ALB|NLB|ECS|EKS|SQS|SNS|ElastiCache|Redshift|Glacier|CloudWatch|CloudTrail|WAF|Shield|Cognito|Secrets\s?Manager|Auto\s?Scaling|Elastic\s?Beanstalk|API\s?Gateway|Step\s?Functions|Glue|Athena|EMR)\b/i;
     export function buildScenarioTools(userModel: UserModel) {
       return {
         readDomainScores: tool({ description: "Read user's domain scores...", inputSchema: z.object({}), execute: async () => userModel.domainScores }),
         listSeenCombinations: tool({ description: "List seen combinations...", inputSchema: z.object({}), execute: async () => userModel.seenCombinations }),
         validateScenario: tool({ description: "Validate scenario...", inputSchema: z.object({ targetDomains: z.array(z.string()), problemStatement: z.string(), weakestDomain: z.string() }), execute: async ({ targetDomains, problemStatement, weakestDomain }) => { /* validation */ } }),
       };
     }
     ```

   - **`agents/scenarioAgent.ts`** — Uses `callLLMWithTools`, new signature `(config, userModel)`, `stripFences` applied.
     ```typescript
     import { callLLMWithTools } from "@/lib/llm";
     import { buildScenarioPrompt } from "@/prompts/scenarioAgent";
     import type { ScenarioOutput, SessionConfig, UserModel } from "@/lib/types";
     function stripFences(raw: string): string {
       return raw.replace(/^```(?:json)?\s*/i, "").replace(/\s*```$/, "").trim();
     }
     export async function scenarioAgent(config: SessionConfig, userModel: UserModel): Promise<ScenarioOutput> {
       const systemPrompt = buildScenarioPrompt();
       const raw = await callLLMWithTools(systemPrompt, [{ role: "user", content: `Generate a ${config.difficulty} scenario.` }], userModel, { temperature: 0.9 });
       try { return JSON.parse(stripFences(raw)) as ScenarioOutput; }
       catch { throw new Error(`scenarioAgent: failed to parse LLM response as JSON. Raw: ${raw.slice(0, 500)}`); }
     }
     ```
     **IMPORTANT**: Will need updating to pass `config.role` and `config.counterpartRole` to `buildScenarioPrompt` in multi-role implementation.

   - **`agents/debriefAgent.ts`** — Two-step pipeline with internal `ExchangeAnalysis` type, `stripFences` applied to both parse calls.

   - **`agents/orchestrator.ts`** — Updated signature: `startSession(config: SessionConfig, userModel: UserModel)`.

   - **`prompts/scenarioAgent.ts`** — `buildScenarioPrompt()` takes no args currently. Will change to `buildScenarioPrompt(role, counterpartRole)` in multi-role.

   - **`prompts/meetingAgent.ts`** — Currently `buildMeetingPrompt(scenario, exchangeCount)`. Will gain counterpart-aware persona block.

   - **`prompts/debriefAgent.ts`** — Two functions: `buildExchangeAnalysisPrompt(scenario)` and `buildDebriefPrompt(scenario, exchangeAnalysis: string)`.

   - **`app/api/scenario/route.ts`** — Accepts `{ config, userModel }`, has input guard, calls `startSession(config, userModel)`.

   - **`app/page.tsx`** — Sends userModel snapshot, userId persists across sessions. Currently hardcodes `role: "solutions-architect"`. Will gain role + counterpart pickers.

   - **`components/Brief/BriefCard.tsx`** — Will gain counterpart-aware label ("Your client" / "You're explaining to" / "You're being asked by" / "Your audience").

   - **`lib/types.ts`** — Current state:
     ```typescript
