};

export type UserModel = {
  userId: string;
  certs: Partial<Record<CertId, CertProgress>>;
};
```

`Partial` because a user may only ever practice 2 of the 5 certs — no need to pre-initialize all of them. `readUserModel` initializes a fresh `CertProgress` (all domains at 50) the first time a cert is accessed.

`DomainScores` as a named type goes away — it's now `Record<string, number>` inside `CertProgress`.

